# Blank — UI structure

Minimal app shell; no blocks/widgets staging.

## Git branches

| Branch | Layout |
|--------|--------|
| `main` | Hero — top nav, no sidebar |
| `sidebar` | Classic sidebar + header + mobile sheet |
| `dashboard` | Full app reference (auth, panel, cabinet) |

```
internal/ui/
  layout/       # shell, header, sidebar, helpers — permanent app chrome
  components/   # dumb reusable pieces (icon, toggles)
internal/views/
  *.templ       # route pages (home, sample, …)
  partials/     # shell head assets, header trailing glue
  models.go     # LayoutData, page structs
internal/site/
  feature.go    # routes, locale wiring, static nav
internal/fixtures/
  locale/*.json # i18n copy
```

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/ui/layout` | Sidebar, mobile sheet, header, theme toggle |
| `internal/ui/components` | Props-only UI; no HTTP or fetch |
| `internal/views` | Compose layout + resolved fixture strings |
| `internal/site` | HTTP routes and layout data assembly |

**views** receive resolved strings/structs only — no `fixtures.LoadLocale` inside `.templ`.

When adding a page: extend `fixtures.Locale` + every `locale/*.json`, add nav in `site/feature.go`, add `internal/views/<page>.templ`, register route in `site/feature.go`.
